<!-- SLIDE 2 / GUARD -->
<section class="hero-slide" data-tone="guard" aria-label="GMS ARC Guard"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="hero-top eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> GMS / ARC GUARD — ELECTROMAGNETIC RESILIENCE</div><h1 class="hero-title"><span>Keep the</span><span><em>signal.</em></span><span>Lose noise.</span></h1><p class="hero-lead">A protected pathway for power, data and sensing. Shielding, filtering, grounding and interface engineering designed around the disturbance that actually matters.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#/products/guard">Explore ARC Guard <span class="arrow">↗</span></a><a class="text-link secondary-link" href="#/platform">See the system architecture ↗</a></div><div class="hero-meta">02 / 04 — PROTECTION IS AN ENGINEERING DISCIPLINE</div></div><div class="hero-vis" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 850 750"><defs><linearGradient id="s2a" x1=".1" y1=".1" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="var(--surface-gold)"/><stop offset=".4" stop-color="var(--brand-gold-light)"/><stop offset=".68" stop-color="var(--art-blue-mid)"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--art-navy)"/></linearGradient><filter id="shadow2"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="20"/></filter></defs><ellipse cx="464" cy="615" rx="235" ry="34" opacity=".17" fill="var(--art-navy)" filter="url(#shadow2)"/><g class="float"><g transform="translate(435 365) rotate(-24)"><path d="M0-254 224-130 224 132 0 255-224 132-224-130Z" fill="url(#s2a)" stroke="var(--art-gold-light)" stroke-width="4"/><path d="M0-194 175-96 175 99 0 196-175 99-175-96Z" fill="var(--surface-gold)" opacity=".86"/><path d="M0-130 115-64 115 66 0 133-115 66-115-64Z" fill="var(--art-blue-mid)"/><circle r="70" fill="var(--art-white)"/><circle r="34" fill="var(--art-blue)"/></g></g><g fill="none" stroke="var(--art-blue)" stroke-opacity=".2" stroke-width="2" class="sway"><ellipse cx="441" cy="364" rx="335" ry="155" transform="rotate(-25 441 364)"/><ellipse cx="441" cy="364" rx="369" ry="195" transform="rotate(-25 441 364)"/></g></svg></div></div></section>
<!-- SLIDE 3 / FLUX -->
<section class="hero-slide" data-tone="flux" aria-label="GMS ARC Flux"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="hero-top eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> GMS / ARC FLUX — THERMAL-AWARE DESIGN</div><h1 class="hero-title"><span>Heat is</span><span>part of the</span><span><em>design.</em></span></h1><p class="hero-lead">Compute power only matters if a system can sustain it. ARC Flux brings package geometry, heat pathways, materials and interconnect decisions into one design conversation.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button" href="#/products/flux">Discover ARC Flux <span class="arrow">↗</span></a><a class="text-link secondary-link" href="#/platform">Explore the architecture ↗</a></div><div class="hero-meta">03 / 04 — PERFORMANCE FOLLOWS PHYSICS</div></div><div class="hero-vis" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 850 750"><defs><radialGradient id="s3a"><stop stop-color="var(--art-white)"/><stop offset=".3" stop-color="var(--art-gold-light)"/><stop offset=".58" stop-color="var(--brand-gold)"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--art-navy)"/></radialGradient><linearGradient id="s3b" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="var(--art-white)"/><stop offset=".6" stop-color="var(--art-blue-light)"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--art-navy)"/></linearGradient><filter id="shadow3"><feGaussianBlur stdDeviation="24"/></filter></defs><ellipse cx="460" cy="630" rx="230" ry="38" fill="var(--art-navy)" opacity=".16" filter="url(#shadow3)"/><g class="float" transform="translate(425 370)"><g transform="rotate(-22)"><rect x="-236" y="-196" width="472" height="390" rx="85" fill="url(#s3b)"/><rect x="-196" y="-160" width="394" height="315" rx="68" fill="var(--art-blue-light)"/><rect x="-159" y="-125" width="317" height="252" rx="51" fill="url(#s3a)"/><rect x="-97" y="-75" width="195" height="150" rx="34" fill="var(--art-blue)"/><rect x="-47" y="-38" width="95" height="76" rx="20" fill="var(--art-navy)"/><path d="M-250 0H250M0-210V205" stroke="var(--art-white)" stroke-width="3" opacity=".33"/></g></g><g fill="none" stroke="var(--brand-gold)" stroke-opacity=".29" stroke-width="2"><ellipse cx="430" cy="358" rx="340" ry="204" transform="rotate(-22 430 358)"/><ellipse cx="430" cy="358" rx="385" ry="235" transform="rotate(-22 430 358)"/></g></svg></div></div></section>
<!-- SLIDE 4 / BRIDGE -->
<section class="hero-slide" data-tone="bridge" aria-label="GMS ARC Bridge"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy"><div class="hero-top eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> GMS / ARC BRIDGE — LIFECYCLE CONTINUITY</div><h1 class="hero-title"><span>Future</span><span>without</span><span><em>erasure.</em></span></h1><p class="hero-lead">Modernization does not always mean replacement. Preserve the value of long-life platforms with authorized interface adaptation, component migration and verifiable compatibility.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-cream" href="#/products/bridge">Explore ARC Bridge <span class="arrow">↗</span></a><a class="text-link secondary-link" href="#/engineering">See sustainment pathways ↗</a></div><div class="hero-meta">04 / 04 — MAKE EVERY GENERATION COUNT</div></div><div class="hero-vis" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 850 750"><defs><linearGradient id="s4a" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="var(--art-gold-light)"/><stop offset=".4" stop-color="var(--brand-gold)"/><stop offset=".7" stop-color="var(--art-blue-mid)"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--art-navy)"/></linearGradient><linearGradient id="s4b" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1"><stop stop-color="var(--art-blue-light)"/><stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--art-blue)"/></linearGradient></defs><g class="float" transform="translate(430 367)"><g transform="rotate(-23)"><rect x="-204" y="-230" width="408" height="460" rx="65" fill="none" stroke="var(--art-gold-light)" stroke-width="44"/><rect x="-169" y="-193" width="338" height="386" rx="48" fill="url(#s4a)"/><rect x="-119" y="-137" width="238" height="275" rx="31" fill="var(--art-navy)"/><rect x="-88" y="-102" width="177" height="205" rx="28" fill="url(#s4b)"/><rect x="-45" y="-52" width="90" height="105" rx="16" fill="var(--art-white)"/></g></g><ellipse cx="430" cy="367" rx="344" ry="238" transform="rotate(-23 430 367)" fill="none" stroke="var(--art-blue)" stroke-opacity=".25"/></svg></div></div></section>
</div></div><div class="hero-controls"><div class="hero-controls-inner container"><span class="hero-counter" id="heroCounter">01 / 04</span><div class="hero-progress" id="heroProgress" role="group" aria-label="Select system showcase slide"><button class="active" aria-label="View slide 1" data-slide="0"></button><button aria-label="View slide 2" data-slide="1"></button><button aria-label="View slide 3" data-slide="2"></button><button aria-label="View slide 4" data-slide="3"></button></div><span class="hero-motion-label">System showcase / 03 sec</span><button class="control-pause" id="heroPause" aria-label="Pause automatic showcase" title="Pause automatic showcase">Ⅱ</button><button class="control-arrow" id="heroPrev" aria-label="Previous slide">←</button><button class="control-arrow" id="heroNext" aria-label="Next slide">→</button></div></div></section>
<div class="marquee"><div class="container marquee-row"><span><i class="dot"></i> GMS / ARC</span><span>Compute × Protection × Thermal × Continuity</span><span class="light">One architecture. Multiple futures.</span></div></div>
<section class="intro container" id="intro"><div class="section-heading"><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> THE PLATFORM</div><h2 class="display">The world demands more from its electronics. <em>We rethink what the electronics can be.</em></h2></div><div class="intro-bottom"><strong>GMS / A DIFFERENT CENTER OF GRAVITY</strong><p>At the center of GMS is a specialized challenge: delivering dependable intelligence at the physical edge, where electromagnetic disturbance, thermal pressure, real-time decisions and the realities of long-lived systems converge. ARC unifies the disciplines that too often meet too late.</p></div></section>
<section class="phenomenon"><div class="container"><div class="phenomenon-head"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> THE ENVIRONMENT DEFINES THE SYSTEM</div><h2>Four forces.<br><em>One response.</em></h2></div><p class="side">Advanced electronics fail or underperform at the boundaries between disciplines. Explore the pressures that shape the ARC architecture.</p></div><div class="threat-grid" id="threatButtons"><button class="threat" data-threat="0" aria-pressed="true"><b>01</b><strong>Uncertain signals</strong><span>Noise, coupling and interface exposure</span></button><button class="threat" data-threat="1" aria-pressed="false"><b>02</b><strong>Constrained compute</strong><span>Timing, power, data and inference trade-offs</span></button><button class="threat" data-threat="2" aria-pressed="false"><b>03</b><strong>Thermal stress</strong><span>Heat paths, package physics and reliability</span></button><button class="threat" data-threat="3" aria-pressed="false"><b>04</b><strong>System longevity</strong><span>Obsolescence and interface continuity</span></button></div><div class="threat-result" aria-live="polite"><h3 id="threatTitle">Protection begins at the interface.</h3><p id="threatCopy">Electromagnetic interference is not one universal threat. Its pathways depend on frequency, enclosure seams, cable entries, grounding, filtering and the host platform. ARC Guard brings those boundaries into the design process from the outset.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="portfolio container"><div class="portfolio-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> THE GMS / ARC FAMILY</div><h2>One platform.<br><em>Four expressions.</em></h2></div><p>Explore four focused solution architectures. Each may stand alone for a specific system problem or work within an integrated customer-defined design.</p></div><div class="portfolio-grid" id="homeProductGrid"><!-- product cards injected by same-file JS --></div><p class="portfolio-note">ARC is a conceptual GMS product architecture and solution-family identity. Specific hardware configurations, production readiness, commercial availability and performance figures require confirmation for each proposed engagement. It is not a claim that standardized modules are stocked or qualified.</p></section>
<section class="vision"><div class="vision-content container"><div class="vision-head eyebrow"><span>GMS / PERSPECTIVE</span><span>DESIGNED FOR TOMORROW'S OPERATING CONDITIONS</span></div><h2>SMALLER.<br>SMARTER.<br><em>Stronger.</em></h2><div class="vision-end"><p>Intelligence should be present where decisions happen. Protection should be designed into the interfaces. Thermal performance should be considered before the package is frozen. And innovation should extend the life of what already matters.</p><a href="#/platform" class="button button-cream">The ARC philosophy <span class="arrow">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
<section class="architecture container"><div class="architecture-head"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> ENGINEERED AS A SYSTEM</div><h2>The intelligence is in <em>the integration.</em></h2></div><p>ARC is not a single component with a futuristic label. It is a coordinated design model: requirements, physical interfaces, processing, heat transfer, electromagnetic behavior, verification and lifecycle decisions work as one.</p></div><div class="arch-diagram"><div class="arch-grid"><div class="arch-node"><small>01 / INPUT</small><b>SENSE</b><span>Sensor and external interfaces</span></div><div class="arch-node"><small>02 / BOUNDARY</small><b>PROTECT</b><span>Power/signal conditioning, filters, isolation</span></div><div class="arch-node"><small>03 / INTELLIGENCE</small><b>PROCESS</b><span>CPU, NPU, GPU or FPGA as needed</span></div><div class="arch-node"><small>04 / PHYSICAL</small><b>MANAGE</b><span>Package, interposer and heat pathway</span></div><div class="arch-node"><small>05 / PLATFORM</small><b>INTEGRATE</b><span>Memory, secure software and host system</span></div></div><div class="arch-ribbon"><div><strong>Electromagnetic resilience</strong><span>Enclosure · Bonding · Return current · Filtering</span></div><div><strong>System assurance</strong><span>Traceability · Cybersecurity · Verification · Configuration control</span></div></div></div><div class="arch-foot"><span class="small">Conceptual architecture. Actual components and verification boundaries are defined by the application.</span><a href="#/platform" class="text-link">Explore the full ARC system ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="sectors"><div class="container"><div class="sectors-head"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> BEYOND A SINGLE INDUSTRY</div><h2>Built around the<br><em>conditions.</em></h2></div><p>Different sectors, shared physical challenges. Explore where rugged intelligence and system continuity create valuable engineering opportunities.</p></div><div id="sectorRows"></div></div></section>
<section class="assurance container"><div class="assurance-head"><div><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> THE STANDARD OF THINKING</div><h2>Precision, not <em>promises.</em></h2></div><p>The strongest technical story is the one that can be examined. GMS approaches each application through defined requirements, controlled configurations, risk-informed design choices and measurable acceptance evidence.</p></div><div class="assurance-grid"><div class="assurance-item"><b>01 /</b><h3>Application first.</h3><p>Target use, environment, interfaces, performance budgets and constraints define the engineering architecture—not the other way around.</p></div><div class="assurance-item"><b>02 /</b><h3>Evidence by design.</h3><p>Plan power, latency, thermal, EMC, functional and environmental verification around the tested configuration and agreed criteria.</p></div><div class="assurance-item"><b>03 /</b><h3>Continuity built in.</h3><p>Document baselines, approved changes, source and supplier traceability, lifecycle dependencies, and realistic recovery paths.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="closing"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow"><i class="dot"></i> DESIGN THE NEXT RELIABLE SYSTEM</div><div class="closing-row"><h2>Make the<br><em>impossible</em><br>practical.</h2><a class="circle-cta" aria-label="Contact GMS" href="#/contact">↗</a></div><p>Explore the ARC family, discuss a specific configuration or engage GMS on a defined custom application. Begin with a non-sensitive requirement outline; detailed technical exchange follows an approved engagement path.</p></div></section>
</main>
